### SCENARIO 3 — a client whose response was lost, retrying as a client actually does.
###
### The client sends a create, the connection drops, and it has no idea whether the row exists. It
### resends the identical request with the identical key. What it must get back is the FIRST
### attempt's result — same id, same Location — and what must NOT happen is a second row.
###
### The count is taken before and after, so "no second row" is measured rather than inferred from a
### status code that would be 201 either way.

# @name CountBefore
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?customer_id=eq.{{CustomerBorovicaId}}&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The attempt whose response the client never sees.
# @name LostAttempt
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: 8f2c1d6a-4b3e-4c8a-9d21-retry-scenario
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8200",
  "title": "Emergency call-out",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "is_emergency": true,
  "quoted_price": 320.00,
  "access_code": "LOST",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerBorovicaId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The retry: byte for byte the same request, the same key.
# @name Retry
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: 8f2c1d6a-4b3e-4c8a-9d21-retry-scenario
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8200",
  "title": "Emergency call-out",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "is_emergency": true,
  "quoted_price": 320.00,
  "access_code": "LOST",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerBorovicaId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### And a third time, because a client that lost two responses retries twice.
# @name RetryAgain
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: 8f2c1d6a-4b3e-4c8a-9d21-retry-scenario
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8200",
  "title": "Emergency call-out",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "is_emergency": true,
  "quoted_price": 320.00,
  "access_code": "LOST",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerBorovicaId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The client finally follows the Location it was given, as it would have after the first attempt.
# @name FollowLocation
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}{{Retry.response.headers.Location}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### THE STATE OF THE WORLD: exactly one more row than before, whatever the client did.
# @name CountAfter
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?customer_id=eq.{{CustomerBorovicaId}}&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
